    <div class="letter">
      <span class="eyebrow">Why OneMRR exists</span>
      <h2 class="h2" id="story-h">Built because we needed it ourselves.</h2>
      <p>I run <strong>Ticket Spot</strong>, an event ticketing app sold on the Shopify App Store, the Wix App Market and directly through Stripe. Each platform reports revenue its own way, so "what's our MRR?" meant three dashboards, a payout spreadsheet and a lot of copying.</p>
      <p>The second question was harder: <strong>why are organizers leaving?</strong> By the time a cancellation showed up, the organizer had usually stopped creating events weeks earlier. I wanted to see that drop while there was still time to ask if they needed help, and to hear from the ones who left anyway.</p>
      <p>So OneMRR does both. It gives you one number for revenue that you can trust and explain, and it helps you notice and follow up when customers drift. It shows its work and labels anything it estimates.</p>
      <div class="sig">
        <span class="mono" aria-hidden="true">CM</span>
        <span><b>Chris McCaw</b><br />Founder of OneMRR and Ticket Spot</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
